//   An mret or sret instruction is used to return from a trap in M-mode or S-mode, respectively.
//     When executing an xret instruction, if the new privilege mode is y, then ELP is set to the
//     value of xpelp if yLPE (see FCFIACT) is 1; otherwise, it is set to NO_LP_EXPECTED; xpelp is
//     set to NO_LP_EXPECTED.
//
// Context:
//   ELP after the xret is observed at its target: a landing-pad fault at a non-lpad when ELP=1,
//     none at lpad 0. yLPE is the new mode's enable: menvcfg.LPE for S, senvcfg.LPE for U and VU,
//     henvcfg.LPE for VS. The other modes' enables are set opposite, so using the wrong one is
//     caught. xPELP=0 after the xret is checked where it is observable: an sret to the same mode
//     (S, and VS with H). mret is in the _Sm file.
//
